caption: <$hgsd.realm-picker>
title: hgsd.realm-picker widget
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Introduction
A plain realm `<$select>` bound to a state tiddler — the one-line way to give any surface "let the user pick a realm into my state". The shipped Capture sidebar uses it for the effective realm (`Default realm:`); the review sidebar does not (list scoping is the multi-select realm-selection checkboxes).

Not to be confused with `<$hgsd.pick>`: the realm-picker is a compact bound select with no popup, no search, and no candidate filtering — when those are needed, use `$hgsd.pick` with a realm `list-filter`/`realm-scope`.

! Attributes

|!Attribute |!Default |!Description |
|state-tiddler |`$:/state/hypergsd/effective-realm` |State tiddler the select writes the chosen realm name to |

The empty option writes `""` (labelled by `$:/language/hypergsd/Widgets/RealmPickerNone`), so an unset picker leaves new items unscoped rather than synthesising a `Realm` tag. Options are the `$:/GSD/Realm/` tags, sorted by title.

! Historical
The single-realm-model parameters (`show-match`, `show-filter-mode`, `show-exclude`) were removed on 2026-08-30 with the multi-select realm model and will not return. The widget was briefly retired on 2026-09-01 and restored the same day — it is documented public surface for sub-plugin authors.

! Example
<$hgsd.realm-picker state-tiddler="$:/state/hypergsd/effective-realm"/>